.TH WREX-TCP 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-tcp \- tcp layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fItcp\fR \fB--tcp\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fItcp\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
TCP (RFC 9293): 20\-byte fixed header plus options. data_off autofilled from options length (explicit wins; <5 kept, flagged only under \-\-strict). flags aggregate settable as bit names (syn,ack,...) or raw int; per\-bit subpaths \-\-tcp\-flags\-syn exist. checksum over the pseudo\-header (v4 RFC 9293 / v6 RFC 8200 §8.1, family follows the network\-layer parent) plus segment and payload. options grammar: eol,nop,mss:1460,ws:7,sackok,sack:L,R,..., or hex:BYTES — or the settable opt.N.* record paths (tranche 22a: \-\-tcp\-opt\-0\-kind mss \-\-tcp\-opt\-0\-mss 1460, one record per option, the dns an.0.* precedent; mutually exclusive with the grammar).
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 30; stacks on ipv4, ipv6, hopopts, routing, frag, dstopts, ah (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --tcp-sport).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-sport=\fIINT\fR\fR
source port Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-dport=\fIINT\fR\fR
destination port Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-seq=\fIINT\fR\fR
sequence number Type u32. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-ack=\fIINT\fR\fR
acknowledgment number Type u32. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-data_off=\fIINT\fR\fR
data offset in 32\-bit words (autofill: derived) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\fR
flag aggregate [cwr,ece,urg,ack,psh,rst,syn,fin]; subpaths flags.<bit> Type flagset. Default: 0.
Bit names (MSB first): cwr, ece, urg, ack, psh, rst, syn, fin. Aggregate \fB\-\-tcp\-flags\fR sets the whole unit; per-bit \-\-tcp\-flags\-cwr sets one bit.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-window=\fIINT\fR\fR
window (autofill: 64240) Type u16. Default: 64240.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-checksum=\fIINT\fR\fR
checksum over pseudo\-header+segment (autofill: computed) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-urgent=\fIINT\fR\fR
urgent pointer Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-options\fR
options: eol,nop,mss:1460,ws:7,sackok,sack:L,R,…, or hex:… (mutually exclusive with the opt.N.* record paths) Type bytes. Default: .

.SH "RECORD SECTIONS"
Repeated record sections; dissected fields carry indexed paths (opt.0.field).

.TP
\fBopt\fR (settable)
TCP options (RFC 9293 §3.1 + the common extensions): one record per option, crafted through index paths opt.0.*, … (the dns an.0.* precedent; deeper indices ride the spec JSON). Typed fields per kind — mss/ws/sack/ts_val/ts_ecr — raw covers tfo/mptcp/unknown kinds; len autofills from the value (explicit kept verbatim, the deliberate\-invalid rule). Dissect\-side the wire truth; eol ends the walk, padding after it stays in the options region.
  kind (str; default ). option kind: eol|nop|mss|ws|sackok|sack|ts|mptcp|tfo or a bare number (required per record)
  len (u8; default 0). option length in bytes incl. kind+len (autofill: derived from the value; explicit kept verbatim — eol/nop carry no length byte)
  mss (u16; default 0). max segment size (kind mss, 0..65535)
  ws (u8; default 0). window scale shift (kind ws, 0..14)
  sack (str; default ). sack blocks as L,R,… relative sequence numbers (kind sack)
  ts_val (u32; default 0). timestamp value (kind ts)
  ts_ecr (u32; default 0). timestamp echo reply (kind ts)
  raw (bytes; default ). raw option data after kind+len (tfo/mptcp/unknown kinds — the wire truth)

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex craft \-\-format hex \-\-layer eth \-\-layer ipv4 \-\-layer tcp \\\\
  \-\-ipv4\-src=127.0.0.1 \-\-ipv4\-dst=127.0.0.1 \\\\
  \-\-tcp\-sport=1234 \-\-tcp\-dport=80 \-\-tcp\-flags=syn,ack

